                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f5fdc919-c0a0-3639-8c01-eeabff1c29d8",
                        "entry_id": "5bdf3eef-7824-37f9-b260-88230afa7c37",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dishonest; based on fraud or deception."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e92c3058-72b5-47c3-94bd-ddacf93d456e",
                                "sense_id": "f5fdc919-c0a0-3639-8c01-eeabff1c29d8",
                                "text": "Secondly, Philoſophy which we are warned not to take heed of : not that Philoſophy, which is true & ſound knowledge attained by naturall diſcourſe of reaſon ; but that Philoſophy which to bolſter hereſie or error, caſteth a fraudulent ſhew of reaſon vpon things which are indeed vnreaſonable, & by that meane as by a ſtratageme ſpoyleth the ſimple which are not able to withſtand ſuch cunning."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f92be264-ed87-48e0-be58-5db4be66053b",
                                "sense_id": "f5fdc919-c0a0-3639-8c01-eeabff1c29d8",
                                "text": "The only reaſon, why men are not always ſufficiently ſenſible of This ; ſo that Many, who are very Juſt in their Dealings between Man and Man, will yet be very fraudulent or rapacious with regard to the Publick ; is becauſe, in this latter caſe, ’tis not ſo obviouſly and immediately apparent uppon Whom the Injury falls, as it is in the caſe of Private Wrongs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1dd9eeff-6959-4e47-841e-0b7c1a8b7d38",
                                "sense_id": "f5fdc919-c0a0-3639-8c01-eeabff1c29d8",
                                "text": "One writer gravely assures us that Maurice of Saxony learned all his fraudulent policy from that execrable volume [The Prince]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "950c1386-e049-364e-b091-4d9aac959125",
                        "entry_id": "5bdf3eef-7824-37f9-b260-88230afa7c37",
                        "glosses": [
                            "False, phony."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff2b897e-423c-4db2-b3f4-b67c82ddbed8",
                                "sense_id": "950c1386-e049-364e-b091-4d9aac959125",
                                "text": "He tried to pass a fraudulent check."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
